gh they had flash.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2022-07-08","toughness":null,"type_line":"Artifact"},{"cmc":0.0,"color_identity":[],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"banned","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{X}{X}","name":"Walking Ballista","oracle_id":"4b515bb0-f275-4400-8032-3173b799ab40","oracle_text":"This creature enters with X +1/+1 counters on it.\n{4}: Put a +1/+1 counter on this creature.\nRemove a +1/+1 counter from this creature: It deals 1 damage to any target.","power":"0","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2020-08-07","toughness":"0","type_line":"Artifact Creature \u2014 Construct"},{"cmc":0.0,"color_identity":[],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"","name":"Wastes","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","oracle_text":"{T}: Add {C}.","power":null,"produced_mana":["C"],"released_at":"2025-08-01","toughness":null,"type_line":"Basic Land"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Because Wastes is a basic land, you can include as many of them as you like in your Constructed decks.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"In Limited events (including Sealed Deck and Booster Draft), Wastes must be in your card pool to be included in your deck. You can't add Wastes to your card pool in the same way that you can add other basic lands.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Wastes is not a land type. If something asks you to name a land type, you can't choose Wastes.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Activated abilities contain a colon. They're generally written \"[Cost]: [Effect].\" Some keyword abilities (such as equip and eternalize) are activated abilities and will have colons in their reminder text. Triggered abilities (starting with \"when,\" \"whenever,\" or \"at\") of noncreature permanents are unaffected by the last ability of Overwhelming Splendor.","oracle_id":"1099588c-cc26-4523-8bd2-90e1e1433f53","published_at":"2017-07-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"An activated mana ability is one that produces mana as it resolves, not one that costs mana to activate. A loyalty ability is an ability of a planeswalker whose cost specifies how many loyalty counters to give or remove.","oracle_id":"1099588c-cc26-4523-8bd2-90e1e1433f53","published_at":"2017-07-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Effects that modify a creature's power and/or toughness, such as the effect of Titanic Growth, will apply to the creatures no matter when they started to take effect. The same is true for any counters that change their power and/or toughness.","oracle_id":"1099588c-cc26-4523-8bd2-90e1e1433f53","published_at":"2017-07-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Overwhelming Splendor leaves the battlefield at the same time as a creature enchanted player controls, any \"when [this creature] [dies or leaves the battlefield]\" abilities of that creature won't trigger.","oracle_id":"1099588c-cc26-4523-8bd2-90e1e1433f53","published_at":"2017-07-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a noncreature permanent becomes a creature, it will lose all abilities it has. However, if the effect that makes that permanent a creature grants it an ability, it will continue to have that ability. For example, the enchanted player's Riddleform will have flying once it becomes a creature.","oracle_id":"1099588c-cc26-4523-8bd2-90e1e1433f53","published_at":"2017-07-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an effect grants a creature an ability after Overwhelming Splendor has become attached to its controller, that creature won't lose that ability.","oracle_id":"1099588c-cc26-4523-8bd2-90e1e1433f53","published_at":"2017-07-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Overwhelming Splendor overwrites all previous effects that set a creature's base power and toughness to specific values. Any power- or toughness-setting effects that start to apply to a creature after Overwhelming Splendor becomes attached to its controller will overwrite this effect. For example, the enchanted player's Riddleform will become a 3/3 creature if player casts a noncreature spell.","oracle_id":"1099588c-cc26-4523-8bd2-90e1e1433f53","published_at":"2017-07-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"While the enchanted player can still activate mana abilities and loyalty abilities, creatures that player controls won't normally have any of those abilities to be activated.","oracle_id":"1099588c-cc26-4523-8bd2-90e1e1433f53","published_at":"2017-07-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a creature enters the battlefield under enchanted player's control, any \"when [this creature] enters the battlefield\" abilities of that creature won't trigger. Any \"as [this creature] enters the battlefield\" or \"[this creature] enters the battlefield with\" abilities won't be applied.","oracle_id":"1099588c-cc26-4523-8bd2-90e1e1433f53","published_at":"2017-09-29","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a creature with an {Q} ability hasn't been under your control since your most recent turn began, you can't activate that ability, unless the creature has haste.","oracle_id":"44f3241f-af82-4f2e-b15d-7f279bf6e816","published_at":"2008-05-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the permanent is already untapped, you can't activate its {Q} ability. That's because you can't pay the \"Untap this permanent\" cost.","oracle_id":"44f3241f-af82-4f2e-b15d-7f279bf6e816","published_at":"2008-05-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"When you activate an {Q} ability, you untap the creature with that ability as a cost. The untap can't be responded to. (The actual ability can be responded to, of course.)","oracle_id":"44f3241f-af82-4f2e-b15d-7f279bf6e816","published_at":"2008-05-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A casting cost of {X}{X} means that you pay twice X. If you want X to be 3, you pay {6} to cast Walking Ballista.","oracle_id":"4b515bb0-f275-4400-8032-3173b799ab40","published_at":"2020-08-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Walking Ballista has been dealt damage or had its toughness reduced by an effect, this limits how many times you'll be able to remove +1/+1 counters from it in a single turn. For example, if it has three +1/+1 counters on it and has been dealt 1 damage this turn, it will be destroyed immediately after you activate the ability a second time and you won't be able to activate it a third time.","oracle_id":"4b515bb0-f275-4400-8032-3173b799ab40","published_at":"2020-08-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The controller of Vedalken Orrery can cast nonland artifact, creature, enchantment, and sorcery cards any time they could cast an instant. This includes on other players' turns and during the upkeep step, draw step, combat phase, and end step.","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2004-12-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This applies only to casting spells. It does not, for example, change when you may activate abilities that can only be activated \"any time you could cast a sorcery\".","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Creatures with the changeling ability will still lose all creature types even though they don't lose changeling.","oracle_id":"71de5f9a-73e4-4a93-b199-b280687f71eb","published_at":"2021-09-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Effects that modify a creature's power and/or toughness, such as the effect of Titanic Growth, will apply to the affected creatures no matter when they started to take effect. The same is true for any counters that change their power and/or toughness.","oracle_id":"71de5f9a-73e4-4a93-b199-b280687f71eb","published_at":"2021-09-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The decision whether or not to tap or untap is made on resolution. This is not a modal spell.","oracle_id":"773ad2ef-5acc-49ea-8d85-056330e87039","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not a toggle effect. If you use Twiddle to tap a card and before it takes effect your opponent taps it, Twiddle will not automatically untap the card.","oracle_id":"773ad2ef-5acc-49ea-8d85-056330e87039","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Activated abilities contain a colon. They\u2019re generally written \u201c[Cost]: [Effect].\u201d Some keywords are activated abilities and will have colons in their reminder text.","oracle_id":"81728b98-8cf9-4734-a318-69184bb4d15c","published_at":"2016-06-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Act of Treason can target any creature, even one that's untapped or one you already control.","oracle_id":"9d08af23-9f4a-4097-9abc-3b17475ab744","published_at":"2019-07-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Gaining control of a creature doesn't cause you to gain control of any Auras or Equipment attached to it.","oracle_id":"9d08af23-9f4a-4097-9abc-3b17475ab744","published_at":"2019-07-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not modal. If the target changes from an artifact to an enchantment or vice versa, this still destroys it.","oracle_id":"a7e97fa9-4b72-4548-b854-5be5f18a6f1a","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an effect causes Dress Down to become a creature, it will lose its own abilities along with all other creatures. This includes the triggered ability that causes it to be sacrificed at the beginning of the end step.","oracle_id":"c1cbbda0-e02b-4b9c-8669-ea87ca629520","published_at":"2021-06-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an effect grants a creature an ability after Dress Down has entered the battlefield, it won't lose that ability. For example, if a land becomes a creature while Dress Down is on the battlefield, it will still gain any abilities given to it by the effect that animated it. It will, however, lose any abilities it already had.","oracle_id":"c1cbbda0-e02b-4b9c-8669-ea87ca629520","published_at":"2021-06-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If, during the enchanted player\u2019s declare attackers step, a creature they control is tapped, is affected by a spell or ability that says it can\u2019t attack, or hasn\u2019t been under that player\u2019s control continuously since the turn began (and doesn\u2019t have haste), then it doesn\u2019t attack. If there\u2019s a cost associated with having the creature attack, the player isn\u2019t forced to pay that cost, so it doesn\u2019t have to attack in that case either.","oracle_id":"cc6f2b79-8fcd-4542-904b-943c7493b8ad","published_at":"2011-09-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The enchanted player still chooses which player or planeswalker each creature they control attacks.","oracle_id":"cc6f2b79-8fcd-4542-904b-943c7493b8ad","published_at":"2011-09-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"In the Two-Headed Giant format, you still only have to pay once per creature.","oracle_id":"e828b189-0e8f-43b8-b909-4c23e742e028","published_at":"2007-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Unless some effect explicitly says otherwise, a creature that can't attack you can still attack a planeswalker you control.","oracle_id":"e828b189-0e8f-43b8-b909-4c23e742e028","published_at":"2014-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Dryad Arbor is changed into another basic land type (such as by Sea's Claim), it continues to be a creature and a Dryad.","oracle_id":"e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71","published_at":"2011-09-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Although originally printed with a characteristic-defining ability that defined its color, this card now has a color indicator. This color indicator can't be affected by text-changing effects (such as the one created by Crystal Spray), although color-changing effects can still overwrite it.","oracle_id":"e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71","published_at":"2013-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Dryad Arbor is played as a land. It doesn't use the stack, it's not a spell, it can't be responded to, it has no mana cost, and it counts as your land play for the turn.","oracle_id":"e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Due to its color indicator (appearing to the left of its type line), Dryad Arbor is green. Color indicators apply in all zones, not just the battlefield.","oracle_id":"e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Forest is a land type and Dryad is a creature type.","oracle_id":"e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Dryad Arbor is changed into another basic land type, it continues to be a green Dryad creature.","oracle_id":"e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a Dryad Arbor gains flash, or you have the ability to play Dryad Arbor as though it had flash (due to Teferi, Mage of Zhalfir or Scout's Warning, for example), you can ignore the normal timing rules for when during your turn you can play a land, but not any other restrictions. You can't play Dryad Arbor during another player's turn, and you can't play Dryad Arbor if you don't have any land plays remaining.","oracle_id":"e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
